// Increment 3: the heavy constant-radius turning fixture.
//
// `docs/benchmark-matrix.md` fixes `CC-HEAVY`'s declared reference as an
// analytic straight/constant-radius envelope. This fixture is the
// constant-radius rung: two concentric quarter-circle guide paths about the
// origin, one per heavy mode, authored the only way `paths[].points` can
// declare a curve — as the chord polyline of the arc (24 chords, so the
// compiled reference and the analytic `CompiledReferencePath::arc` agree to
// the chord tolerance the Increment 1 `narrow_isolated_curve_v2` fixture
// fixes).
//
// | path | centre | radius | start angle | sweep |
// | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
// | `bus_arc_path` | `(0, 0)` | 40 m | `0` | `+pi/2` (counter-clockwise) |
// | `truck_arc_path` | `(0, 0)` | 44 m | `0` | `+pi/2` (counter-clockwise) |
//
// Each heavy template authors the Increment 3 axle geometry — a wheelbase and
// a maximum steering angle — so the compiler's turning-limit check sees a
// genuine geometric radius. The bus (6.0 m wheelbase, 0.3 rad steering limit)
// can hold `tan(0.3) / 6.0` and the rigid truck (5.0 m, 0.3 rad) `tan(0.3) /
// 5.0`; both exceed the fixture's `1 / 40 m` and `1 / 44 m`. Tightening either
// geometry below the facility curvature makes `validate_v2` reject the
// document with `E_FACILITY_CURVATURE`, which the fixture's test exercises.
//
// Every authored body dimension and desired speed is constant (`min == max`),
// so a realized body identifies its template. Each mode has its own facility
// and demand source, so the two heavy bodies never interact and the run is an
// isolated free-flow turn. The bodies are held to the facility's lane: no
// corner of any body leaves the 4.0 m lane, which is the "bodies never clip
// through a curb" contract at the geometry level the compiler admits.
{
  schema_version: 2,
  id: 'heavy_turning_v2',
  coordinate_system: { x: 'east_m', y: 'north_m' },
  paths: [
